  "linear:fig:omega": {
    "number": "2.2",
    "page": "27",
    "title": "Upper bounds for the exponent $\\omega $ of matrix multiplication, from Strassen's $\\log _27\\approx 2.807$ (1969) to $2.3713$ (2024). Since Coppersmith and Winograd (1990), all progress has come from the same ``laser method'', refined: $2.3755$, then $2.3729$ (2012), $2.37286$ (2014), and, after three smaller steps, $2.37134$ (2024). These bounds are quoted, not proved here. The lower bound is still $\\omega \\ge 2$",
    "anchor": "figure.caption.5"
  },
