  "fig:specz": {
    "number": "5.1",
    "page": "74",
    "title": "After Mumford: the spectrum of $\\Z [x]$. The bottom line is $\\operatorname {Spec}\\Z $. Above each prime $p$ stands the fibre $\\operatorname {Spec}\\mathbb F_p[x]$, a vertical line made of the generic point $(p)$ and the closed points $(p,f)$, one for each monic irreducible $\\bar f$ modulo $p$, of which a few are drawn in grey. The curve is the closure of the point $(x^2+1)$: it meets the fibre at $p$ in two points $(p,x\\pm a)$ when $p\\equiv 1\\pmod 4$, in one point $(p,x^2+1)$ of degree $2$ when $p\\equiv 3\\pmod 4$, and has its two branches meeting at the single point $(2,x+1)$ of the fibre at $2$, where $x^2+1=(x+1)^2$",
    "anchor": "figure.caption.8"
  },
