  "fig:cubicclass": {
    "number": "6.1",
    "page": "96",
    "title": "The real points of the cubic $E\\colon y^2=x^3-x+1$. The line $y=1-2x$ meets $E$ at $P=(0,1)$, $Q=(1,-1)$ and $R=(3,-5)$, so the ideal it generates in $\\C [x,y]/(y^2-x^3+x-1)$ is $\\mathfrak m_P\\mathfrak m_Q\\mathfrak m_R$. The vertical line $x=3$ gives $(x-3)=\\mathfrak m_R\\mathfrak m_{R'}$ with $R'=(3,5)$. In the class group, $[\\mathfrak m_P][\\mathfrak m_Q]=[\\mathfrak m_{R'}]$: the chord-and-tangent addition of points",
    "anchor": "figure.caption.9"
