    "title": "Weight diagrams of two representations of $U(3)$, drawn in the plane $\\mu _1+\\mu _2+\\mu _3=\\text {constant}$. Left: $V_{(2,1,0)}$, of dimension $8$: the six permutations of $(2,1,0)$, and the weight $(1,1,1)$ with multiplicity $2$ (the circled centre); restricted to $SU(3)$, this is Gell-Mann's ``eightfold way'' of 1961, in which the eight lightest baryons fill the weights. Right: $V_{(3,0,0)}=\\operatorname {Sym}^3\\C ^3$, of dimension $10$, whose tenth weight, at a corner of the triangle, was a particle not yet observed; Gell-Mann predicted it in 1962, and the $\\Omega ^-$ was found at Brookhaven in 1964",
